      "text": "Partitioning uses the distributive property: multiplying a sum gives the same result as multiplying each part and adding the partial products. Hundreds stay hundreds, tens stay tens, and ones stay ones until we regroup. Picture three equal rows with four counters in each. Splitting each row into two and two does not change the twelve counters.",
      "chapter": "Build the idea",
